  "name": "DLC- Differential Leucocytes Count",
  "code": "DLC",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><br></p><table><thead><tr><th><div>DLC Component</div></th><th><div>Normal Range</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Neutrophils</div></td><td><div>40-80% of total WBC count</div></td><td><div>Neutrophil levels within the normal range indicate a healthy immune response. Deviations from the normal range may suggest infection, inflammation, or other underlying conditions.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Lymphocytes</div></td><td><div>20-40% of total WBC count</div></td><td><div>Lymphocyte levels within the normal range indicate a balanced immune system. Abnormal levels may be associated with viral infections, immune disorders, or certain medications.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Monocytes</div></td><td><div>2-10% of total WBC count</div></td><td><div>Monocyte levels within the normal range indicate a normal immune response. Elevated levels may indicate chronic infections, autoimmune diseases, or certain cancers.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Eosinophils</div></td><td><div>1-6% of total WBC count</div></td><td><div>Eosinophil levels within the normal range indicate a balanced immune response. Increased levels may suggest allergies, parasitic infections, or certain autoimmune conditions.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Basophils</div></td><td><div>0-1% of total WBC count</div></td><td><div>Basophil levels within the normal range indicate a normal immune response. Elevated levels are relatively rare but may be seen in certain allergic reactions or hematological disorders.</div></td></tr></tbody></table><p><br></p>",
